From 3d999008bbeba87ec57bfb993396f7d3922c13da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harrison Short <kagadar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:08:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland.drv: Add initial systray support

D-Bus SNI will be used if available on the system.
If D-Bus is not available we fall back to letting explorer handle the
icon. D-Bus is dynamically loaded to avoid making it a hard runtime
dependency.

Communication with D-Bus is handled by extending the wayland event loop
to handle two additional FDs; one for new application-side events (icon
added, modified, removed) and one for D-Bus side events, which will
only be enabled once an icon is added.

Connection to D-Bus happens on a dedicated thread; icon updates are
added to an internal list and synchronised once the connection is
established.

Should support all valid icon formats.

This implementation does not attempt to handle NIF_INFO.
